# AragonAgent - ignored paths.
#
# Two rules matter more than the rest:
#   1. every generated `dist/` is ignored EXCEPT the documentation site, which is
#      committed on purpose (see the "shipped documentation site" block);
#   2. nothing below relies on a machine-local git config.

# ---- Dependencies ---------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
dist/
packages/*/dist/

# ---- Shipped documentation site (deliberately committed) ------------------
# `docs/guide-doc` cannot be built in this repository: its accuracy gate extracts
# truth sets from the private engine sources, so the site ships prebuilt. The
# broad `dist/` rule above would swallow it. Git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is still excluded, so the directory itself is re-included
# first and its contents second. Both lines are required - drop either one and
# the site silently disappears from the tree.
!docs/guide-doc/dist/
!docs/guide-doc/dist/**

# The generator's scratch output: build.mjs renders into dist.tmp before the
# atomic rename, and the phase tests render into .tmp-test-*.
docs/guide-doc/dist.tmp/
docs/guide-doc/.tmp-test-*/

# ---- TypeScript incremental build info ------------------------------------
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Desktop app packaging / test / benchmark output ----------------------
# Reports and failure artifacts, never source.
packages/desktop/build-staging/
packages/desktop/release/
packages/desktop/release-e2e/
packages/desktop/test-results/
packages/desktop/bench-results/
packages/desktop/pack-logs/

# ---- Local state and secrets ---------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
coverage/

# ---- OS cruft -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---- Editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~
